4:["$","article",null,{"className":"mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-12 sm:px-8","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-sm text-slate-500","children":[["$","$L8",null,{"className":"transition hover:text-cyan-200","href":"/","children":"Home"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"/"}],["$","$L8",null,{"className":"transition hover:text-cyan-200","href":"/blog","children":"Blog"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"/"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-slate-300","children":"Tax Invoice Explained: Format, Rules & Examples"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-wrap gap-2","children":[["$","span","Tax Invoice",{"className":"rounded-full bg-white/8 px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-cyan-200","children":"Tax Invoice"}],["$","span","GST",{"className":"rounded-full bg-white/8 px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-cyan-200","children":"GST"}],["$","span","Compliance",{"className":"rounded-full bg-white/8 px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-cyan-200","children":"Compliance"}]]}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"mt-5 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl","children":"Tax Invoice Explained: Format, Rules & Examples"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-300","children":"Complete tax invoice guide for India: meaning, format, sample, examples, GST rules, PDF, Excel templates, mistakes and FAQs."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 text-sm text-slate-500","children":["26 May 2026"," · ",22," min read · ","InvoiceWala Team"]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-10","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"prose prose-invert max-w-none prose-headings:tracking-tight prose-a:text-cyan-300","children":[["$","h2","0",{"className":"mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold text-white","children":"What is a Tax Invoice?"}],["$","p","1",{"className":"mt-4 text-base leading-8 text-slate-300","children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"A tax invoice is an invoice issued for a taxable supply of goods or services. It records the seller, buyer, invoice number, invoice date, item description, taxable value, tax rate, tax amount and final amount payable. In India, the term tax invoice is closely connected with GST because GST registered businesses issue tax invoices for taxable supplies."}]]}],["$","p","2",{"className":"mt-4 text-base leading-8 text-slate-300","children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The meaning is simple: a tax invoice tells the customer what they are being charged for and shows the tax included in the transaction. It is more formal than a casual bill because it contains tax details and business identifiers. A professional tax invoice helps both sides maintain clean records."}]]}],["$","p","3",{"className":"mt-4 text-base leading-8 text-slate-300","children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The purpose of a tax invoice is not only payment collection. It also supports GST compliance, customer accounting, vendor records, payment tracking and business reporting. For B2B buyers, a correct tax invoice can matter for Input Tax Credit records. If the invoice has the wrong GSTIN, missing HSN/SAC, incorrect tax amount or duplicate invoice number, it may create extra work for the buyer and seller."}]]}],["$","p","4",{"className":"mt-4 text-base leading-8 text-slate-300","children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Tax invoices are used in many business situations. A freelancer may issue a tax invoice for design or development work. A consultant may invoice monthly advisory fees. A contractor may bill labor and material. A retail store may issue a product invoice. An ecommerce seller may create invoices for online orders. A service business may invoice installation, maintenance or repair work."}]]}],["$","p","5",{"className":"mt-4 text-base leading-8 text-slate-300","children":["$La"]}],"$Lb","$Lc","$Ld","$Le","$Lf","$L10","$L11","$L12","$L13","$L14","$L15","$L16","$L17","$L18","$L19","$L1a","$L1b","$L1c","$L1d","$L1e","$L1f","$L20","$L21","$L22","$L23","$L24","$L25","$L26","$L27","$L28","$L29"